{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.H2CompanionRep","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2CompanionRep","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.H2GramArithmetic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_det_eq_unit_mul_qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_det_eq_unit_mul_qFactorial","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L87-L100","doc":"**The regular-rep Gram determinant is `[2]_q · [2]_q!` (sorry-free).**\nExhibits the \"up to a unit\" in `det(Gram) = [n]_q!` *concretely* at\n`n = 2`.  The regular trace form differs from the symmetrizing form by\nthe unit `[2]_q = 1 + q` (nonzero at generic `q`), so\n\n  `det = [2]_q² = (1 + q)·(1 + q) = [2]_q · [2]_q!`.\n\nThis is the `n = 2` witness of the shape consumed by\n`QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_gram_det_eq_qFactorial`\n(unit `c = 1 + q`), confirming the general `det(Gram) = c·[n]_q!`\ninterface fires at the base rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_det_ne_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_det_ne_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L80-L85","doc":"**`H_2` semisimple ⟺ nonzero regular-Gram determinant ⟺ `[2]_q! ≠ 0`\n(sorry-free).**  Wenzl's criterion at `n = 2`, from the regular\nrepresentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_det","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L73-L78","doc":"**`det(Gram) = [2]_q²` from the regular representation (sorry-free).**\nComposes `h2GramFromRep_eq` with the arithmetic determinant\n`h2GramMatrix_det` — the `n = 2` case of `det(Gram) = [n]_q!` (up to a\nunit), now grounded in the regular representation of `H_2(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep_eq","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L63-L71","doc":"**The representation-computed Gram equals the asserted Gram\n(sorry-free).**  Each entry `tr(ρ(eᵢ)ρ(eⱼ))` reduces, via the\ncompanion matrix, to the literal that `H2GramArithmetic.h2GramMatrix`\nhad asserted: `tr(I) = 2`, `tr(C) = q-1`, `tr(C²) = q²+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramFromRep","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L58-L61","doc":"**The regular-trace Gram matrix** built from the representation:\n`Gᵢⱼ = tr(ρ(eᵢ) · ρ(eⱼ))`.  The trace is the observation step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2Rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2Rep","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The representation `ρ : H_2(q) basis → M₂(K)`, `1 ↦ I`, `σ ↦ C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2Companion_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2Companion_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L44-L53","doc":"**The companion matrix satisfies the Hecke relation (sorry-free):**\n`C² = (q-1)·C + q·I`.  Hence `σ ↦ C` is a genuine representation of\nthe Hecke generator — the left regular representation of `H_2(q)` —\nso every trace below is a real regular-representation trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2Companion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2Companion","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2CompanionRep.lean#L38-L42","doc":"**Left multiplication by `σ` on `H_2(q)`** in the basis `{1, σ}`: the\ncompanion matrix of `X² - (q-1)X - q`.  Column `0` is `σ·1 = σ`\n(coordinates `(0, 1)`); column `1` is `σ·σ = q·1 + (q-1)·σ`\n(coordinates `(q, q-1)`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}